   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize Jaime Laczko to elect to participate in the optional\ntwenty-five year retirement plan for forest rangers in the service of the\ndepartment of environmental conservation",
    "basePrintNo": "S8292",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8292-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8292\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize Jaime Laczko to elect to partic-\nipate in the optional twenty-five year retirement plan for forest\nrangers in the service of the department of environmental conservation\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes Jaime Laczko to elect to participate in the optional 25 year\nretirement plan for forest rangers.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1- Authorizes Jaime Laczko to file an application with the State\nComptroller to participate in the retirement plan established under\nsection 383-c of the retirement and social security law. The bill\nfurther provides that his application must be filed within one year of\nthe effective date of this act.\n\nSection 2- Provides that all past costs associated with implementing the\nprovisions of this act be borne by the state of New York\n\nSection 3- Contains the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nForest Ranger Jaime Laczko was placed in the Police and Fire retirement\nplan 375-H rather than the 383-C plan option. At the time forest rangers\nwere made police officers in 2006 they were given the option to transfer\ninto the Police and Fire Retirement System. Ranger Laczko's intent was\nto be placed in the 383-C plan which would allow him to retire after 25\nyears of service.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2015-16: S2231 Referred to Civil Service; A5135 Referred to Governmental\nEmployees\n2014: S6493 Referred to Civil Service; A8711 Referred to Governmental\nEmployees\n2013: S3181 Passed; A5012 Passed; 2013 Veto Memo 204\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\n$3,900 increase in the annual contributions of the State of New York for\nthe fiscal year ending March 31, 2019. In addition, there will be an\nimmediate past service cost of $102,000 which would be borne by the\nstate of New York as a one-time payment.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
